dockerfile-fix2: preserve priv/ dir when copying test_lanes.exs
==================================================================
Date: 2026-08-09
Commit: fix(docker): preserve priv/ dir when copying test_lanes.exs
Related: cb59b9b (wrong first fix), Railway deployment a71aedf2 (failed build)

ROOT CAUSE
----------
mix.exs:152 runs `Code.eval_file("priv/test_lanes.exs")` at project-config
load time (from WORKDIR /app in the builder stage). The file must therefore
exist at `/app/priv/test_lanes.exs` BEFORE `mix deps.get` runs (step 6/17),
because the mix aliases (`test_lanes`) are evaluated while the Mix project
is loading.

The previous fix (cb59b9b) changed the COPY instruction to:

    COPY mix.exs mix.lock priv/test_lanes.exs ./

Per the Dockerfile reference semantics, when a COPY has MULTIPLE sources,
each source's BASENAME is used as the path in the destination:
`priv/test_lanes.exs` was therefore copied to `/app/test_lanes.exs` (basename
`test_lanes.exs`), NOT `/app/priv/test_lanes.exs`. The directory component of
the source path (`priv/`) is NOT preserved by a multi-source COPY.

Result: `mix deps.get` step failed with
`** (Code.LoadError) could not load /app/priv/test_lanes.exs. Reason: enoent`
exactly as seen in the a71aedf2 build log (step 5/17 COPY ok, step 6/17 deps.get failed).

THE FIX (exact diff)
--------------------
@@ -40,10 +40,14 @@ ENV MIX_ENV="prod"

 # install mix dependencies
 # mix.exs aliases read priv/test_lanes.exs at project-config load (via
-# Code.eval_file), so that single compile-time file must be present before
-# mix deps.get. Only the one file is copied here (not the whole 62MB priv/
+# Code.eval_file, resolved relative to /app), so that single compile-time file
+# must be present at /app/priv/test_lanes.exs before mix deps.get. A multi-
+# source COPY (mix.exs mix.lock priv/test_lanes.exs ./) would drop the file's
+# basename into /app, losing the priv/ path component; copy it explicitly into
+# priv/ instead. Only the one file is copied here (not the whole 62MB priv/
 # corpus, which lands later via `COPY priv priv`).
-COPY mix.exs mix.lock priv/test_lanes.exs ./
+COPY mix.exs mix.lock ./
+COPY priv/test_lanes.exs priv/
 RUN mix deps.get --only $MIX_ENV
 RUN mkdir config

No other line changed. The later `COPY priv priv` (full 62MB corpus) and the
release copy remain untouched.

COPY SEMANTICS REASONING (Dockerfile reference, docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/#copy)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. `COPY priv/test_lanes.exs priv/`
   Single source file, destination ENDS WITH A TRAILING SLASH => dest is a
   DIRECTORY. The source's basename (`test_lanes.exs`) is placed INSIDE it,
   producing `/app/priv/test_lanes.exs`. Correct path for `Code.eval_file`.

2. `COPY mix.exs mix.lock ./`
   Both basenames (`mix.exs`, `mix.lock`) land in WORKDIR `/app`. Correct.

Why the old single line failed: with multiple `<src>` and dest `./`, Docker
takes each source's basename and concatenates it onto the dest. There is NO
directory-component preservation for the third source; `priv/` is dropped.
This is the classic `COPY subdir/file.txt ./` => `basename-in-cwd` behavior.

VERIFICATION APPROACH
---------------------
- No docker daemon on this box (`docker version` Server section absent;
  "cannot connect"). `docker buildx` is installed (v0.31.1) but a build
  requires a reachable daemon, which is not available; per instructions we
  did NOT attempt to start dockerd.
- Verification therefore rests on Docker reference semantics (cited above)
  plus the observed failure mode in the a71aedf2 build log, which is fully
  consistent with the basename-in-dest explanation (file present at /app
  but Code.load fails on /app/priv/test_lanes.exs).
- A local `mkdir priv && cp` repro would have hidden the bug (the cp would
  place the file at the right path locally); it was deliberately NOT used.

Status: semantics verified by Docker reference reasoning; build to be
confirmed by the next Railway deployment triggered by this push.
